// Kit
@1 = ~black dragon disciple~
@2 = ~Black Dragon Disciple~
@3 = ~BLACK DRAGON DISCIPLE: The blood of a black dragon runs in the veins of these sorcerers. As they grow in power, the dragon within slowly takes over their body, from black claws to leathery wings.

Advantages:
- Hit Die: d6 instead of d4, and THAC0 progression of a druid.
- 1st level: +1 bonus to AC. Gains Draconic Claws.

DRACONIC CLAWS: The nails of the Black Dragon Disciple have curved into vicious claws like those of a black dragon. They deal 1d4 slashing damage and allow 2 attacks per round when fighting unarmed.

- 2nd level: Gains Swamp Stride.

SWAMP STRIDE: Affinity with swamp terrain allows the Black Dragon Disciple to move freely through it. He is immune to the effects of spells such as Entangle, Grease and Web.

- 3rd level: May use Breath Weapon once per day.

BREATH WEAPON: The Black Dragon Disciple exhales a 15-ft. long, 5-ft. wide line of acid, dealing 4d4 acid damage to all creatures in the line (save vs. Breath for half).

- 4th level: Gains Acid Affinity. Claws now deal 1d6 slashing damage and count as +1 magical weapons.

ACID AFFINITY: The black dragon's blood protects the Black Dragon Disciple from acid and makes his own acid more potent. He gains 20% acid resistance, and all acid damage he deals is increased by 5%. Both increase at levels 8, 12 and 16, up to 80% acid resistance and +20% acid damage. At level 20, he becomes immune to acid and his acid damage is increased by 25%.

- 5th level: +1 bonus to AC and Constitution.
- 6th level: Gains a bite attack, summoned as an off-hand weapon while unarmed, dealing 1d6 piercing and 2 acid damage. The bite counts as a magical weapon of the same enchantment as the claws. The innate abilities Fight with the Bite and Fight without the Bite summon or dismiss it at will.
- 7th level: May use Breath Weapon twice per day. Damage increases to 6d4.
- 8th level: Acid Affinity improves. Claws now deal 1d8 slashing damage and count as +2 magical weapons.
- 9th level: Gains Draconic Tail.

DRACONIC TAIL: The Black Dragon Disciple grows a powerful tail. Each round, one creature within 5 ft. must save vs. Breath or take 1d10 crushing damage and be knocked prone for 1 second.

- 10th level: +1 bonus to AC. Gains the Blindsense passive ability.

BLINDSENSE: The Black Dragon Disciple can perceive his surroundings without relying on sight. He becomes immune to blindness and can see and target invisible creatures.

- 11th level: May use Breath Weapon three times per day. Damage increases to 8d4.
- 12th level: Acid Affinity improves. Claws now deal 1d10 slashing damage and count as +3 magical weapons.
- 13th level: Bite now deals 2d6 piercing damage and 2d4 acid damage.
- 14th level: Gains Draconic Wings.

DRACONIC WINGS: The Black Dragon Disciple grows a pair of draconic wings, gaining +4 movement speed, +2 AC and immunity to critical hits. The wings occupy the helmet slot and may be toggled on and off at will.

- 15th level: +1 bonus to AC and Constitution.
- 16th level: Acid Affinity improves. Claws now deal 2d6 slashing damage and count as +4 magical weapons.
- 17th level: May use Breath Weapon four times per day. Damage increases to 10d4.
- 18th level: Gains the innate ability Frightful Presence.

FRIGHTFUL PRESENCE: The Black Dragon Disciple radiates an aura of draconic menace. Enemies of a lower level than the Black Dragon Disciple within 15 ft. must save vs. Spell or be panicked for 2 rounds. Whether it succeeds or fails, a creature then becomes immune to this aura for 24 hours. Allies are not affected. The aura may be toggled on and off at will.

- 19th level: Breath Weapon damage increases to 12d4, and the line grows to 30 ft. long and 10 ft. wide.
- 20th level: Draconic Apotheosis: +1 bonus to AC and immunity to sleep and paralysis. Acid Affinity reaches its peak. Claws now deal 2d8 slashing damage and count as +5 magical weapons.

- High-level abilities (Throne of Bhaal): besides the sorcerer's extra spells and Summon Dark Planetar, the Black Dragon Disciple may learn the innate abilities of an adult black dragon: Breathbloom, Wing Buffet, Insect Swarm and Plant Growth; he may also summon a black dragon turtle or a black draco-sphinx.

Disadvantages:
- Casts one fewer spell per day at each spell level.
- Casts spells as a sorcerer one level lower (minimum 1st level). For example, he gains access to 2nd-level spells at level 5 instead of 4.
- Cannot use any weapon: the Black Dragon Disciple fights only with his claws and bite. His proficiency points may only be spent on Single Weapon Style (up to 1 point) and Two-Weapon Style (up to 3 points).
~

// Draconic Claws (item, one description per stage: levels 1, 4, 8, 12, 16, 20)
@10 = ~Draconic Claws~
@11 = ~Draconic Claws

The nails of the Black Dragon Disciple have curved into black claws.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d4 (slashing)
Attacks per round: 2
Speed Factor: 2
Not magical~
@12 = ~Draconic Claws

The claws have hardened and darkened.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +1
Damage: 1d6+1 (slashing)
Attacks per round: 2
Speed Factor: 2
Counts as a +1 weapon for the purpose of hitting creatures~
@13 = ~Draconic Claws

The claws have grown longer and sharper.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +2
Damage: 1d8+2 (slashing)
Attacks per round: 2
Speed Factor: 2
Counts as a +2 weapon for the purpose of hitting creatures~
@14 = ~Draconic Claws

The claws have become as hard as a dragon's.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d10+3 (slashing)
Attacks per round: 2
Speed Factor: 2
Counts as a +3 weapon for the purpose of hitting creatures~
@15 = ~Draconic Claws

The claws have grown to the size of a young dragon's.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +4
Damage: 2d6+4 (slashing)
Attacks per round: 2
Speed Factor: 2
Counts as a +4 weapon for the purpose of hitting creatures~
@16 = ~Draconic Claws

The claws have become those of an adult black dragon.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +5
Damage: 2d8+5 (slashing)
Attacks per round: 2
Speed Factor: 2
Counts as a +5 weapon for the purpose of hitting creatures~

// Draconic Bite (off-hand item, one description per stage: levels 6, 8, 12, 13, 16, 20)
@19 = ~Draconic Bite~
@20 = ~Draconic Bite

The jaw of the Black Dragon Disciple has lengthened into a draconic maw. The bite is his off-hand weapon: it gives one more attack per round, with the usual two-weapon penalties, which Two-Weapon Style reduces. It can be dismissed with the innate ability Fight without the Bite, to fight with the claws alone.

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +1
Damage: 1d6+1 (piercing) + 2 acid
Speed Factor: 2
Counts as a +1 weapon for the purpose of hitting creatures~
